meta {
  name: Cross-Tenant Lookup
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/patients/cross-tenant-lookup?phone=9876543210
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  phone: 9876543210
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data.match && data.match.person && data.match.person.id) {
    bru.setEnvVar("crossTenantPersonId", data.match.person.id);
  }
}

docs {
  Look up a mobile number across ALL tenants via the shared, platform-level
  `Person` identity (globally-unique phone). Used by order creation when no
  existing patient is selected, to detect a patient already registered at another
  business BEFORE a duplicate is created. Captures `crossTenantPersonId` from the
  match (for the Import From Person request).

  ## Query

  - `phone` (required) — the raw mobile number. Normalized server-side (non-digits
    stripped, trailing 10 digits kept) and matched EXACTLY (not fuzzy), which
    limits enumeration. Only valid 10-digit numbers (first digit 6-9) are looked
    up; anything else returns `{ match: null }`.

  ## Response `data`

  - `{ "match": null }` — no cross-tenant identity for that number.
  - `{ "match": { person, ownerTenant, existsInCurrentTenant } }`:
    - `person` — the shared identity (full details, by design): `id`,
      `platformMrn`, name parts, `gender`, `bloodGroup`, `dateOfBirth`, `phone`,
      `email`, `address`, `aadhaarNumber`, `panNumber`, emergency contact.
    - `ownerTenant` — the business that first registered the person
      (`id`, `name`, `shortName`, `email`, `phone`, `logoUrl`), or `null`.
    - `existsInCurrentTenant` — `true` when the caller's tenant already has this
      patient (the operator should just select it; no import needed).

  ## Notes

  - Reads only the non-RLS `persons`/`tenants` tables plus a tenant-scoped
    `patients` existence check — no tenant isolation is bypassed.
  - Available to any authenticated business user (no extra permission).
}
